Input image 1 is the approved visual identity reference. Preserve its exact cast, faces, costumes, muted gouache and ink, worn paper texture, brass pin joints and tragic French travelling theatre mood. This is flat hand-painted cardboard artwork, front-facing orthographic, not a photograph or a 3D render. Soft neutral illumination painted into the surface, no cast shadow on the background. No text, labels, numbers, watermark, logo, scenery, ground, strings or rods unless expressly requested. Genuine transparent alpha background, not a white or checkerboard drawing. Keep every separate item completely apart with broad clear gutters. No cropped paint at edges.
A FOUR PART detachable leg sheet for the female dancer with chestnut bun, thoughtful sorrowful face, faded deep petrol-blue short scalloped ballet dress, cream stockings and ballet slippers. Exactly FOUR fully disconnected vertical leg segments arranged as a 2 by 2 grid. TOP LEFT: left THIGH from round hip cap to brass-pin knee cap, pointing straight down. TOP RIGHT: right THIGH from round hip cap to knee cap, straight down. BOTTOM LEFT: left SHIN from round knee cap down to ankle and complete shoe, foot pointing a little left. BOTTOM RIGHT: right SHIN from round knee cap down to ankle and complete shoe, foot pointing a little right. Thighs 320 pixels high, shins WITH shoes 390 pixels high. Dancer has cream stockings and worn ivory ballet slippers; clown has loose charcoal trouser legs and brown soft work shoes. Knee has round overlap so it bends physically. No torso, head, whole body, arms, labels or scenery. At least 60 pixels transparency between pieces.